# --- never commit: credentials and session state -----------------------
# Chrome profiles: each holds Cookies, Login Data, and (Indeed's) the
# Cloudflare clearance it depends on. Keep them locally (see README), never
# publish them. The glob covers the per-source directories -- Naukri and
# Indeed get one each so they can be scraped at the same time -- because
# `.browser-profile/` alone does not match `.browser-profile-naukri/`, and
# 38MB of cookie jar was one `git add .` from being published.
.browser-profile/
.browser-profile-*/
*.cookies
cookies.txt
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials*.json
secrets*.json

# --- local data, not source -------------------------------------------
jobfeed.db
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
jobfeed.log
*.log
nohup.out

# --- python -----------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# --- editors / os -----------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# --- ruflo (local tooling, never committed) ----------------------------
# Everything `ruflo init` generates stays on this machine: its Claude Code
# config, skills, agents, commands, runtime state and SQLite memory store.
# Anchored to the repo root (leading /) -- unanchored `CLAUDE.md` would also
# swallow frontend/CLAUDE.md, which is Next.js's own generated file, not ruflo's.
/CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.claude-flow/
.agents/
.swarm/
/.mcp.json
